  {:id :prediction-error :defines :eps :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:o :mu]
   :formal "eps_k := o_k - mu_k" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 error terms (reduction: no generalised coordinates)" :lean "machineChannelPredictionError" :lean-status :closed
   :lean-note "CARRIER DECLARED 2026-09-05 by :F8 leg 1 slice 2 (this row previously read :lean nil :lean-status :missing). mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/MachinePredictionError.lean declares machineChannelPredictionError as the producer the implementation runs (free_energy.clj:203-278, compute-prediction-error under :prediction-error/v1), and MachinePredictionErrorWitness.lean proves eight scored reference values and five typed outcomes, every one matching production EXACTLY (runs/F8-prediction-error/clojure-readback.txt, delta 0.0 on all eight scored, 5/5 typed). Both modules elaborate with 0 errors and 0 warnings and #print axioms gives [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] on all 50 declarations, no sorryAx. THE :formal LINE ABOVE IS NOT THE WHOLE PRODUCER, and three reductions it does not carry are stated in Lean rather than in prose. (1) THE PRODUCER IS NOT A FUNCTION INTO R. It returns one of three typed records -- present, absent, refused -- and which one it returns is the decision (AC1, Joe 2026-09-02 on C130 s2). refusalDominatesAbsence: an unobserved channel whose likelihood ALSO failed is REFUSED, not omitted, so a tick's omission count is not its count of unobserved channels; absence_requires_wellFormedModel is the converse. (2) THE SUBTRACTED TERM IS NOT mu. It is :predicted-mean, a member of the likelihood output belief/predict-observation computes from the belief state (belief.clj:1199-1238); the implementation's belief is an entity-indexed CATEGORICAL map, not the per-channel Channel -> R mean this :formal line and Holes.BeliefState both assume, and the per-channel mean is a READOUT of it (belief.clj:640-737). registryFormOfPresent states exactly where this line holds: on a channel whose predicted mean IS the belief mean. Whether that holds of the running stack is a question about predict-observation and is NOT claimed here. (3) A REFUSAL OF ONE CHANNEL REFUSES THE WHOLE UPDATE (war_machine.clj:6110-6127): an absent channel is omitted and the rest are scored, but a single refusal empties the error map for every channel (oneRefusalEmptiesTheUpdate); and eps is attempted on only the EIGHT channels with a likelihood model (belief.clj:933-934), the other six producing no record at all (channelsWithoutLikelihood, verified equal to the Clojure set by the readback). THE FINDING, PROVED NOT ASSERTED: A NEGATIVE PREDICTED VARIANCE IS SCORED, NOT REFUSED. prediction-member (free_energy.clj:191-201) checks FINITENESS and not sign, so -4.0 is :present; the max at :270 then floors it to min-variance, giving the LARGEST per-call precision the floor allows (100 under the declared default) and a record indistinguishable from one built on a variance of exactly zero except by reading :predicted-variance back out (negativeVarianceIsNotRefused, subMinVarianceIsFloored, zeroAndNegativeVarianceAgree). A SECOND FINDING, THE ONE LEG 2 WILL CONSUME: the :precision this producer stamps is 1/max(predicted-variance, min-variance), derived from the LIKELIHOOD's variance for this one call, and is NOT R7's Pi, which is derived from the channel's ERROR HISTORY. They occupy the same :precision key at different points in one tick -- precision/weighted-error (precision.clj:213-233) overwrites the first with the second and preserves it as :per-call-precision. Measured on one channel in one tick (readback section 3): the producer stamps 4.0 and weighted-error 2.0; after the overwrite the same keys read 1.6 and 0.8, and 1.6 is 8/5, MachinePrecisionWitness.halfError from slice 1. The Lean module therefore names its field perCallPrecision: spelling it precision would reproduce the bare-symbol collision leg 2's concordance checker exists to refuse. NOT A RULING -- nothing is written to :choices, and no claim is made about whether the producer should refuse a negative variance or whether the two precisions should share a key. NOT CLAIMED: nothing about generalised coordinates (the reduction :eq already names), nothing about the R3 belief-aggregation driver that consumes these errors, nothing about :policy-free-energy, a different row on the same node. POINTER DEFECT FOUND AND NOT REPAIRED: this row's :code below reads war_machine.clj:4368-4379, which at futon2 HEAD is inside scan-blocks, the Block-footer commit scanner, and has nothing to do with eps. The producer is free_energy.clj:203-278 and the tick's call site is war_machine.clj:6110-6127. :code is the field TN 9a gates, so it is named here and left as it stands."
   :lean-at "mathlib4 1282b75e32 (MachinePredictionError.lean, MachinePredictionErrorWitness.lean; parent e2e8ee9649, slice 1's sha)"
   :code "war_machine.clj:4368-4379"}
  {:id :precision :defines :Pi :node :R7 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:eps :eps0]
   :formal "Pi_k := 1 / max(Var(eps_k), eps0)" :eq nil :lean "machinePrecision" :lean-status :closed
   :lean-note "CARRIER DECLARED 2026-09-05 by :F8 leg 1 slice 1 (this row previously read :lean nil :lean-status :missing). mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/MachinePrecision.lean declares machinePrecision as the map the implementation runs -- min(max(1/max(V,minVariance), floor), cap) with V the regularized error variance over the bounded window -- and MachinePrecisionWitness.lean proves ten reference values, every one matching the production double EXACTLY (runs/F8-precision/clojure-readback.txt, delta 0.0 on all ten). Both modules elaborate with 0 errors and 0 warnings and #print axioms gives [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] on every theorem. THE :formal LINE ABOVE IS NOT THE WHOLE MAP: registryFormOfUnclamped states exactly where it holds -- on histories whose variance component already lies in [floor, cap] -- and MachinePrecisionWitness.registryFormFailsAtTheFloor exhibits a history where it does not. TWO OF THE THREE GUARDS ARE DEAD UNDER THE DECLARED DEFAULTS, proved not asserted: V >= 1/21 > minVariance = 0.01 on every history, so the eps0 branch of this row's own :formal line is never taken (defaultsMinVarianceInert), and Pi <= 21 < cap = 200, so the cap is never taken (defaultsCapInert, defaultsLeTwentyOne). Only the floor 0.1 is reachable, and floorIsReached exhibits a history that reaches it. The inertness is a property of the DEFAULTS and not of the formula: wideWindowReachesMinVariance exhibits a parameter set (window 200, everything else production) under which the minVariance branch does fire. NOT A RULING -- nothing is written to :choices, and no claim is made about whether the two dead guards should change. NOT CLAIMED: no statement about generalised coordinates, about the :salience-mode :summed historical path, or about the need term, which production Pi does not contain."
   :lean-at "mathlib4 e2e8ee9649 (MachinePrecision.lean, MachinePrecisionWitness.lean; parent 824f67b5e2, the sha the U35 receipt of 2026-09-05 was taken at)"
   :note "Var(eps_k) is the bounded rolling variance of channel k's prediction ERROR history (precision.clj:116-135 update-channel-precision: production precision is the variance component of new-error; the observation enters only the separately emitted :salience term under the default :salience-mode :separate). Earlier this row imported :o and said 'variance of o_k' -- corrected 2026-09-01 (C10, found reviewing D5f): at symbol grain R7 imports eps, so the theory edge is R8->R7, and R2->R7 holds only at route grain. In buckley2017 eq. 45 the variances σ are model parameters, not sample statistics; this row is therefore stack-defined in content and only theory-defined in role." :code "precision.clj:116-135, 160-190; war_machine.clj:4380-4388"}
