                        :chosen-form "epistemic(M) = survey-availability(phase(M)) * min(1, EIG(M) / (10 * ln 2)), added as a FOURTH additive factor beside central/strategic/doable. EIG(M) is the sum over M's field questions of the policy-conditioned expected information gain of resolving that question, computed by the canonical kernel epistemic_value.clj:64-90 with its Bayes-coherence gate -- NOT a posterior spread and NOT a gap lookup, which epistemic_value.clj:9-13 refuses by name. Each question is ONE BINARY LATENT READ PERFECTLY, so an unsettled question has prior 0.5 and is worth ln 2 nats and a settled one is worth 0; the degenerate settled case goes through the same kernel via a one-observation model whose posterior IS the prior (mission_epistemic_value.clj:186-205), so the coherence gate applies to every question rather than to the open ones only."
                        :measured "Per resolvable id in :mission/cross-refs, whether that neighbour's :mission/phase is readable, which is what the judge needs to answer 'is this neighbour workable, at or past DERIVE?'; and once per mission, whether :mission/mtime is inside a declared 14-day window. Both come off the code/v05/mission-doc hyperedge that mission-doc-index (war_machine.clj:1450-1474) already fetches -- no new read boundary. On the 2026-09-03 field: 374 hyperedges, all 374 named, 313 with a readable phase; 123 of the 133 candidates :measured, 8 :phase-unreadable, 2 absent from the index."
                        :declared "Four fiats, named as such. (1) The latent is 'workable' = phase at or past DERIVE, read off phase-doability at threshold 0.5 rather than declared a second time (mission_epistemic_value.clj:100-128, pinned equal to war-machine's table by war_machine_test/the-doability-prior-is-pinned-across-the-two-namespaces). (2) The observation model is a perfect reading of that bit. (3) phase-survey-availability, one number per phase: head 0.3, identify 0.6, map 1.0, derive 0.2, argue 0.1, verify 0.0, instantiate 0.0, document 0.1, complete 0.0, with 'unknown' DELIBERATELY ABSENT so an unreadable phase earns no survey credit and says so as a typed absence. (4) reference-open-questions 10, the denominator, which is a CONSTANT and not the mission's own question count -- dividing by n(M) measures the DENSITY of ignorance and on this field it ranked M-metric-harness (one question, open, 0.69 nats) above M-pattern-mining (nine open, 6.24 nats), the thinnest neighbourhood winning the survey. This table is hand-authored exactly like phase-doability; under the ruling that is what it is allowed to be, because it MULTIPLIES measured nats instead of standing in for them."
                        :default-off "default-mission-value-weights is {:central 0.25 :strategic 0.45 :doable 0.30 :epistemic 0.0} (war_machine.clj:2128-2131). At weight 0.0 field-readings returns nil, NO substrate read happens, no field is attached to any candidate, and the recorded numbers are byte-identical -- pinned by war_machine_test/the-epistemic-weight-defaults-to-zero-and-reads-nothing. A three-key weights map is still accepted with :epistemic defaulted to 0.0, so the FUTON_WM_VALUE_WEIGHTS declarations already in use are unaffected; the four must still sum to 1 (mission-value-weights, war_machine.clj:2212-2231)."
                        :evidence "Implementation mission_epistemic_value.clj (316 lines) wired at war_machine.clj:2301-2302 and :2326-2329; tests mission_epistemic_value_test.clj and the U22 block of war_machine_test.clj. Step-through runs/U22-mission-epistemic/ (README.md plus seven EDN files), produced by u22_mission_epistemic.clj: both rankings from the SHIPPED enrich-candidates-with-mission-value on the same 133 candidates, differing only in the weights map. The after-weights keep Joe's option-B ratio among the three exploit factors and shrink them by (1 - 0.15), so value_after = 0.85 * value_before + 0.15 * epistemic * gates * decay -- checked and holding on 133 of 133 rows -- and a common positive factor cannot reorder the exploit part, so every rank move IS the epistemic term. Rank 1 unchanged in both arms (M-zaif-harness-v1). Headline: M-web-arxana-missions, MAP, rank 124 -> 74 on two open questions worth 1.3863 nats; against a LIVE doability factor (arm C, one declared substitution) 102 -> 87, passing fifteen missions closer to delivering."
                        :not-claimed "NO RULING AND NO DEFAULT CHANGE. Nothing here says 0.15 is the right weight or that this question set is the right one; :observed records that the term is now in the code behind a declared input. Three limits, measured rather than hedged. (a) 266 cross-references over 116 missions resolve to no mission the index knows, 39 of them numeric (M-1..M-7 on M-pattern-mining, M-foo/M-bar/M-baz on M-portfolio-inference, M-INC, M-WS): the first run of this term paid ln 2 nats for each and put M-pattern-mining at rank 4 on nine open questions, eight of them scrape artefacts, so unresolvable references are now EXCLUDED and counted, and the ingest that writes :mission/cross-refs is where that belongs. (b) Over the 123 measurable candidates the open-question count is {0 6, 1 108, 2 8, 3 1} -- 108 have exactly one open question and it is their own reading staleness, and only 9 have an unread neighbour -- so on this field the term is close to a staleness ordering with a phase mask and its moves are correspondingly small. The obvious next question kind is already written in the docs (the numbered 'MAP must answer:' lists) and is a follow-on row. (c) NOTHING DOWNSTREAM CHANGES BY DEFAULT: with :epistemic 0.0 the term is not computed at all."
                        :statement "Mission value is pragmatic-only in the shipped default: central and strategic say where a payoff lands, doable says how close the mission is to delivering one, and no factor pays for finding out. The epistemic term is implemented as of 2026-09-03 and reachable through the :mission-value-weights opt or FUTON_WM_VALUE_WEIGHTS, at weight 0.0 by default. Da Costa eq. 42's G is ambiguity + risk - novelty; the mission-grain term here is the novelty side at a grain the theory does not write, so it is a stack specialisation and not a form any retrieved source states."
                        :adjacent-finding "The doability factor itself has been INERT on the futon2 path since 2026-07-19, and the phase is sitting on the hyperedge it already fetched. compute-delta-t-mission (war_machine.clj:2046-2054) resolves phase through futon3c.aif.mission-delta-t, which is not on futon2's classpath, so requiring-resolve returns nil, the {:delta-T 0.0} fallback carries no :mission-phase, and phase-doable takes the 'unknown' 0.3 for every candidate. In the records: :phase is nil on every ranked mission row in every trace file from wm-trace-2026-07-19.edn onward (rows carrying a :doable key, per trace file: 07-17 103 rows / 98 non-nil phases / nine distinct :doable values; 07-18 107 / 99 / nine; then 07-19 106 / 0 / {0.3 106}, 07-21 109 / 0 / {0.3 109}, 08-30 and 08-31 134 / 0 / {0.0 4, 0.3 130}, 09-01 267 / 0 / {0.0 8, 0.3 259}, 09-02 269 / 0 / {0.0 8, 0.3 261}), so on 09-02 :doable is 0.3 on 261 of the 269 rows with the other 8 operator-gated at 0.0. Meanwhile :mission/phase is a prop on the same code/v05/mission-doc hyperedge (mission_delta_t.clj:237-240 reads it off the endpoint vertex) and 313 of 374 carry a readable one. Where both carriers have a reading they AGREE: 123 agree, 0 disagree (runs/U22-mission-epistemic/07-doability-live.edn). So this is a plumbing gap, not a disagreement about phase. NOT REPAIRED HERE -- repairing it would change the default doable of most candidates, which is the silent default change U22 forbids. Written up in C492-mission-epistemic-value.md section 4b; it wants its own row."}
  :survey-mission-epistemic-action
  {:observed :survey-mission-action-type-with-an-eig-leg-implemented-default-off
   :status :decided
   :default-ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-03" :grounds :ruling
                    :channel "J8 walkthrough in session, claude-1 presenting; Joe verbatim: 'j8 stay off (again, for now)'"
                    :decision "Both defaults stay off FOR NOW: the portfolio proposer stays unarmed and default-survey-eig-weight stays 0.0. The accepted grounds: the U4-rerun discipline -- arming the proposer adds ~133 candidates per tick and removes the bootstrap gap candidate, a change that should be introduced as a measured before/after against a baseline corpus of live ticks that does not yet exist. Revisit once the first live-run corpus is on record; the :adjacent-finding (declared-determinism outranking, the C487 coverage gap) should be dispositioned before or with any arming, or the first armed tick will select surveys for the wrong reason."}
   :ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-02" :grounds :ruling
            :where "futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md, rulings 3b (the epistemic-action hole) and 3c (the catalog design)"
            :decision "3b: the machine has no ACTION whose value is finding out -- an epistemic action at mission grain, whose G is dominated by information gain over what the mission has not answered. 3c: the catalog of a mission's cascade record is the substrate such an action would read."
            :consequence "Opened zaif-harness S6; half (a) is wm-contract :U23 (the catalog reader, done) and half (b) is :U24 (implemented 2026-09-03). The DEFAULT FLIP -- arming the portfolio proposer, or giving efe/default-survey-eig-weight a non-zero value -- is NOT ruled and is worklist :J8."}
   :what-existed-before "The action type was declared and empty. predict-effects :survey-mission delegates to :survey (forward_model.clj:180-187), which predicts an EMPTY obs-delta, a variance on one channel, and IGNORES :target; the candidate carried a flat :weight 0.3 (portfolio_action_proposer.clj:72-85); and can-propose? fell through to the :default arm (false), so the machine's only relationship to surveying a mission was a :learn-action-class candidate saying it could not."
   :chosen-form "survey-eig(M) = phase-survey-availability(phase(M)) * SUM_q EIG(q), in NATS, and G(survey-mission M) = G-core(survey) - survey-eig-weight * survey-eig(M). The leg is SUBTRACTED because information gain is preference-increasing -- the sign Holes.G := risk - eig gives it -- and it enters the AUGMENTATION layer, not G-core, because :G-core = risk + ambiguity is invariant I3 (efe.clj:93, :757-760, :814-815). Implementation survey_mission_value.clj:288-326 (the term) and :241-276 (the question set). NATS ARE NOT RESCALED, unlike the U22 mission-value term: that term blends with three dimensionless exploit factors so it is normalized into [0,1]; this leg enters G, where G-risk and G-ambiguity are already nats, so the one declared scalar is a pure exchange rate."
   :dominated-by-information-gain "AN IDENTITY, NOT A MAGNITUDE CLAIM, and the distinction is the entry's point. Because predict-effects ignores :target for this type, all 133 survey candidates on the staged field share ONE :G-core (runs/U24-survey-mission/04-arms.edn: :distinct-G-core 1 against :distinct-survey-eig-nats 7), so every per-target difference between two survey candidates IS the epistemic leg. At the declared 0.02 the leg is 0.152 of a score of 5.302 -- small. Corollary: no weight can reorder two survey candidates; their order is the nats order at every weight, and the weight decides only whether surveying beats advancing. Pinned by survey_mission_value_test.clj:223-242."
   :measured "Two question kinds, both off carriers that already exist. (a) THE MISSION'S UNANSWERED MAP QUESTIONS: the numbered list under a standalone `MAP must answer:` line, the carrier C492 section 4c named. Measured over the 133 candidates on 2026-09-02: ONE doc carries it (futon0 M-apm-capability-ratchet.md line 260, six questions). Four other primary docs contain `must answer` in constructions that are not a MAP question list; they are recorded as :near-miss-phrasings (survey_mission_value.clj:125-140) with pointers and deliberately NOT matched, and a test feeds each to the parser and fails if it matches (survey_mission_value_test.clj:44-56). No per-question answer carrier exists -- the doc's own `MAP findings` sections number Finding 1..n against no question id -- so every listed question is open with basis :no-per-question-answer-carrier and a doc-line pointer, which is an absence with a pointer rather than an assumption. (b) THE KIN-CATALOG GAP: U23's eleven-carrier cascade record (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U23-cascade-catalog/carrier-population.edn), partitioned into five carriers a survey could read and six it could not, each entry carrying U23's own absence reason and corpus count (survey_mission_value.clj:183-233). A carrier the catalog already read is settled and worth 0, so the three missions U23 surveyed score 0 on this half -- including M-zaif-harness-v1, the mission the machine wants, which is the least informative survey target on the catalog half precisely because it has already been surveyed."
   :declared "Four fiats, three of them U22's REUSED rather than re-declared. (1) An open latent sits at 0.5 and (2) is read perfectly, so it is worth ln 2 nats -- mission_epistemic_value.clj:59-71 fiats (a) and (b), and every question here goes through mission_epistemic_value.clj:207-210 -> epistemic_value.clj:64-90, the canonical kernel with its Bayes-coherence gate. (3) phase-survey-availability, mission_epistemic_value.clj:130-145, unchanged; a test fails if a second copy of that table appears (survey_mission_value_test.clj:127-130). (4) THE ONE NEW FIAT: the partition of U23's eleven carriers into five answerable and six not. It is not a judgement about importance -- it is whether a survey of an uncatalogued mission could return a reading OR a typed zero, which is what makes the latent readable at all -- and the six excluded are excluded and COUNTED rather than paid ln 2 each, the same discipline that kept 266 unresolvable cross-references out of U22's score."
   :default-off "Twice over, and measured. (i) :survey-mission is not proposable unless portfolio-action-proposer/*portfolio-proposer-active?* is true, which is false by default and is not wired into war_machine.clj at all (portfolio_action_proposer.clj:131-137). (ii) efe/default-survey-eig-weight is 0.0 (efe.clj:93), at which the :survey-eig key is absent from :augmentation-terms altogether and :controller-score is byte-identical: on the staged field 0 of 278 candidates carry the key and the max score delta against unenriched candidates is 0.000e+00 (runs/U24-survey-mission/04-arms.edn :controls :c-default-off). A candidate carrying NO payload is skipped rather than imputed 0.0 nats, so an unmeasured candidate never records a measured-looking zero (efe.clj:757-760; survey_mission_value_test.clj:216-221)."
   :staged-measurement "runs/U24-survey-mission/, produced by u24_survey_mission.clj, byte-identical on two consecutive runs. The field is data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-09-02.edn line 2 (run 4abad68c-5481-4402-8f0e-252add62c54b), and two controls establish it IS the recorded field: all 146 recorded candidates reproduce their own :G-risk, :G-ambiguity and :controller-score at max delta 0.000e+00, and policy/select-action reproduces the record's own :decision. Arms: recorded 146 -> :advance-mission M-zaif-harness-v1; survey-dark 278 at weight 0.0 -> the same decision; survey-live 278 at the declared 0.02 -> :survey-mission M-apm-capability-ratchet, the one mission with a listed MAP question set. The break point is SOLVED, not searched: a survey candidate takes rank 1 for any weight above 0.004808."
   :adjacent-finding "A :survey-mission candidate outranks an :advance-mission candidate on DECLARED DETERMINISM, not on information gain, and this row's demonstration is built not to ride on it. All 36 real IDENTIFY-phase candidates on the staged field: the survey option outranks its own recorded advance option with the epistemic leg OFF, 36 of 36. predict-effects :survey declares a variance on :mission-health and none on the other thirteen channels, so those thirteen take the 1e-9 floor (efe.clj:56-59) and its ambiguity term is 7.915207 nats better than :advance-mission's -- exactly one channel's worth of declared variance, and exactly the figure C487 section 5 measured on the :fire-pattern / :advance-mission pair. Under G = risk + ambiguity with lower preferred, an action model that declares it knows what will happen is rewarded for saying so. That is upstream of this row and is the same coverage gap C487 section 6 reached from the C-vector side. Pinned by survey_mission_value_test.clj:302-329; recorded as a finding, not a ruling."
   :u4-rerun "The row's acceptance asks for the U4 sweep re-run after the action type exists, as the before/after of whether ambiguity finally discriminates. THE ANSWER IS NO, and the number says how close it came. U4 grain A on the staged field: the EFE-best candidate is unchanged with and without the ambiguity leg on BOTH arms. lambda_break falls from 1.024081 to 1.004631 -- from 2.41 percent of its own size short of flipping the winner to 0.46 percent short -- and the candidate that would overtake changes from :no-op to a survey candidate. C487's C4 positive control (drop RISK instead) fires on both arms, so the zero is a measurement and not a broken detector. The ambiguity term's VALUE SET is unchanged: five distinct values before and after, survey candidates landing at -116.79209997800035, the level :fire-pattern already occupied. The family adds mass at an existing level, not a new level. runs/U24-survey-mission/05-ambiguity-rerun.edn."
   :discharge "The row's statement says the discharge of a survey flight is MAP answers as typed observations at mission grain. That shape is written as data at survey_mission_value.clj:392-419, :status :declared-not-implemented, with what blocks it: U23 measured the flight-discharge carrier as :writer-exists-no-records -- the writer is reachable (futon3c flight_record.clj:347) and there are ZERO *.flight.edn files anywhere under ~/code. No flight record is written by U24 and none exists to write against."
   :not-ruled "Whether the portfolio proposer is armed by default, and what value survey-eig-weight takes if it is non-zero. Both are worklist :J8. Nothing here changes a recorded number: the row's whole behavioural footprint on the default path is zero."}
  :temperature-update {:observed :selection-gain-fold-default-variational-flag-gated :status :decided
                       :ruling {:by "joe" :at "2026-09-01" :grounds :ruling
                                :decision "The current tau -- from selection gain / score spread -- is a shortcut, and the drawn R7->R14 was a conflation of two precision-like scalars (J1: no). Pursue the theory-aligned policy precision: gamma = 1/beta with beta updated from the policies' expected free energy (friston2017 eq. 2.7, over the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) of eq. 2.1), so that the machine's decisiveness is the formalism's, not an engineering proxy."
                                :sources-note "C461 §6 (2026-09-01) corrected two citations claude-1 wrote into the I1 packet: dacosta2020 A.2 supports only gamma's ROLE in selection (sigma(-G) 'can be extended to sigma(-gamma G)', referring to [44] for the update scheme) and is not a source for the beta update; and in eq. 2.7 pi0 = sigma(-gamma . G), the EFE-only distribution (friston2017.txt:684), not the habit prior E. Eq. 2.7's F is the per-policy F_pi (notation table, friston2017.txt:291) -- the same object as parr2022 B.4 -- so the beta update depends on I2's F_pi (J3). Second read (claude-20, 2026-09-01): dropping dacosta2020 A.2 is right, but dropping eq. 2.1 with it over-corrected -- 2.1 is where beta is introduced, as the rate of the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) (friston2017.txt:325-336); 2.7 gives the update, 2.1 gives the prior it is over, so both belong. Also note for anyone diffing this file against a generated figure: the :decision string above, stamped :by joe, was AMENDED after Joe ruled -- its citation list was claude-1's summary wording, not Joe's, and the amendment is C13 plus this second read. Joe's ruling itself (J1: no) is unchanged."
                                :consequence "D4's retirement of R7->R14 stands; no ruling-added edge. Opened H3 (hole: gamma is not the theory's) and I1 (implement beta/gamma dynamics) in worklist.edn."}
                       :evidence "DEFAULT PATH, unchanged: arena-tau-mode war_machine.clj:643-664 returns :selection-gain-only for an unset or unrecognised FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE, its pure parser tau-mode-of at war_machine.clj:627-641; the closed dispatch policy.clj:76-145; selection_gain.clj:173-206 folds realised outcomes, called live at war_machine.clj:4821-4824 (C448 5c.2). VARIATIONAL LAW, realised behind the flag: policy_precision.clj:95-395 (converge-beta, the eq. 2.7 root) and policy_precision.clj:497-561 (carry-beta, the cross-tick beta and its :beta-source); policy.clj:76-145 case :variational-beta-gamma (tau = beta, g and tau_spread both out of the expression); policy.clj:56-74 (temperature-source); war_machine.clj:156-183 (variational-tau-preconditions!, called at war_machine.clj:5035) and war_machine.clj:185-201 (variational-temperature-opts). Persisted: trace.clj:570-581 (:policy-precision-state) and trace.clj:168-178 (the decision, which keeps :tau and :tau-source). Every pointer here re-read at HEAD on 2026-09-01 by C24; the two this field carried before (war_machine.clj:238-248, policy.clj:32-80) had both drifted onto other code and kept resolving, because pointer_check verifies line ranges and not content."
                       :theory-alternative "friston2017 eq. 2.7: β = β + (π - π₀)·G, γ = 1/β -- IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-01 and reachable on the live path as FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=variational-beta-gamma (I1 slice b1 built the solver, futon2 a75f763 + 0fb8b27; I1 (b2c) / RUN8 stage S3 wired it, futon2 5a24194). Still the ALTERNATIVE and not the default, and still not adjudicated against it -- see :realised below."
                       :statement "The mechanism updates tau from realised selection gain (default) or score spread, not by the β/γ precision dynamics. But LIVE: the judge calls fold-realized-outcome every tick (war_machine.clj:4821-4824; the 4332-4361 this line carried until C24 had drifted) and the fold returns the state unchanged unless a well-formed unseen :realized-outcome is present, and that field is absent on today's live path, simulation-only (selection_gain.clj:187-193; C454). So live tau holds at its prior: an update check runs per tick and never fires. 'Fixed-calibrated' described the live behaviour; 'folds realised outcomes' describes the mechanism; both are needed. SINCE 2026-09-01 THAT IS NO LONGER THE WHOLE MECHANISM: a third mode computes tau by the beta/gamma dynamics instead of calibrating a gain, and it is off by default rather than absent. The sentence above still describes what runs when nobody sets the flag."
                       :realised {:at "2026-09-01" :by "I1 slice (b2c), staged and run as RUN8 / stage S3, futon2 5a24194"
                                 :what "gamma = 1/beta, with beta the root of friston2017 eq. 2.7 solved on this tick's field, is now REACHABLE ON THE LIVE PATH as FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=variational-beta-gamma. tau_eff = beta exactly (policy.clj:76-145): the selection gain g and the score-spread calibration tau_spread BOTH leave the expression, so this is a different law and not a third calibration of the same one. This is what the :ruling above said to pursue; what changed is that pursuing it is now a flag rather than a plan."
                                 :default-unchanged "The default is still the selection-gain fold, which is why :observed keeps that name first. arena-tau-mode (war_machine.clj:643-664) returns :selection-gain-only for an unset OR unrecognised FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE, and RUN8's control pre-flight tick -- run8_s3_preflight.clj on the default mode -- recorded tau 1.0, :tau-source :selection-gain-only, and no beta at all (C469-s3-live-tau.md, table at :76-81)."
                                 :run-evidence "GAMMA MOVES TICK TO TICK ON OUR OWN FIELD, from G and pi -- but say which run measured what, because the two are not the same run. THE 20-TICK SERIES IS DARK: runs/2026-09-01-s2/ (RUN7, FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK=1) carries :policy-precision-state on 20/20 records, all :converged? true, :bracketed? true, :beta-source :converged-posterior, with beta 1.0026460727 -> 1.0343423166 and gamma 0.997360910 -> 0.966797920 from a declared beta_0 = 1.0 (runs/2026-09-01-s2/README.md; the same series reprinted at runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt:4,17-36). Nothing consumed it there. LIVE CONSUMPTION WAS MEASURED ON TWO TICKS, not twenty: run8_s3_preflight.clj ran one control tick and one tick under the flag, the latter selecting at tau = beta = 1.0364669814843985 with :tau-source :converged-posterior and gamma 0.9648160702310347. RUN8 deliberately ran no 20-tick S3 stage run and said so (its :reviewer-should-check (6)). So: a 20-tick gamma series exists and a live tau series does not, and no one should read the first as the second."
                                 :fallback "A tick whose solve did not both converge and bracket HOLDS the carried beta -- the last solved posterior, or the declared beta_0 on a cold start -- and does NOT cross to the selection-gain law. The hold is upstream in carry-beta (policy_precision.clj:497-561), and policy.clj:76-145 throws rather than reverting to 1/g when no beta reaches it, because a tau series mixing the two laws is uninterpretable. Which law produced each tick's tau is named per tick by temperature-source (policy.clj:56-74) and persisted with the decision (trace.clj:168-178), so a run may not be reported as N ticks of variational tau without the :converged-posterior count beside it. Named in worklist I1 :slice-b2b (2) BEFORE the wiring was written, as RUN8 :acceptance required."
                                 :measured-effect "On the recorded fields the new law moves the recorded numbers and not the choice. Replaying S1, S1b and S2 under both laws (runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt): 0 controller-rank moves, 0 habit-rank moves, 0 habit-argmax moves and 0 softmax-argmax moves, with mean softmax total-variation distance 0.0003573076 on S1. That is structural rather than lucky for the within-group part -- -G/tau is monotone in G for every tau > 0, so within one ln E value the ordering cannot move -- and measured for the rest: the smallest cross-group adjacent margin was +0.7355590795 (ARMS.txt:14-19). The replay control reproduced each record's own selection at its recorded tau at delta 0.0 before any arm was read."
                                 :not-claimed "NOT ADJUDICATED. No number here says the variational law is better than the selection-gain fold; :observed records that both are now in the code, not that the choice is made. The ln E placement the live path takes ships as the interim of :choices :pi-zero-form, which stays :open-branches. And nothing downstream ACTS on tau: RUN8's :consumer-audit found the only readers of the decision's :tau and :softmax-weights either report (full_loop_runner.clj:2570-2577, not reachable from run_tick_once per RUN6) or persist (trace.clj:175-178). That is a fact about today's code, not a guarantee."}
                       :u2-retrodiction
                       {:by "claude-cli" :at "2026-09-02" :row :U2 :report "C486-u2-tau-retrodiction.md"
                        :script "u2_retrodiction.clj:1-632" :artifact "U2-RETRODICTION.txt"
                        :asked "SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U2 named the vehicle for adjudicating the tau arms: score each arm's policy posterior at tick t against the tick's own recorded next observation, across S2/S3/S4, on the ground that the records carry both halves. They do. The vehicle was run. It does not adjudicate, and the reason is measured rather than asserted."
                        :rule "L_mix(a,t) = ln SUM_i pi_i exp(-F_pi(t+1)_i), the log evidence of the observed next observation under the arm's posterior as mixture weights, reported beside E_F = SUM_i pi_i F_pi(t+1)_i and F_pi(t+1) at the arm's argmax, and bracketed by an ORACLE (all mass on argmin F) and an ANTI-ORACLE (all mass on argmax F) whose gap -- 0.754047 nats on both fields -- is the whole range any score can move in. F_pi is the horizon-one Gaussian observed-data free energy of the tick-t prediction against the tick-(t+1) observation, policy_free_energy.clj:41-151, called live at war_machine.clj:300-305 with :absent-variance :floor."
                        :fields "S2 (runs/2026-09-01-s2, 20 records, 19 scorable transitions) and S4 (runs/2026-09-01-s4, 4 records, 3 transitions). S3 NOT FOUND and recorded as such: runs/2026-09-01-s3 holds ARMS.txt and README.md only, its README first line saying it is a replay and not a 20-tick stage run, and RUN8's two live ticks are pre-flight ticks that are not a consecutive pair. S3 contributes 0 transitions."
                        :controls "Four, all run before any arm was read. (1) SOLVER: the local :none arm reproduces src converge-beta at delta 0.00e+00 on both fields. (2) ALIGNMENT: 19 of 19 and 3 of 3 transitions have the t+1 record's :previous-trace-timestamp equal to tick t's :timestamp, so no posterior is scored against an outcome that is not its own. (3) BRACKET: 0 arm-tick scores fall outside [anti-oracle, oracle]. (4) REPRODUCTION: recomputing F_pi(t+1) from tick t's :ranked-actions and tick t+1's observation reproduces the RECORDED value at max delta 0.000e+00 over 145 candidates x 19 transitions, so this is a reading of the run's own score and not a second implementation of it."
                        :result-tau-law "NOT ADJUDICATED, and this study cannot adjudicate it. The variational arms' posteriors do retrodict better than the default law's -- softmax(-G/tau) at the record's own tau 1.0, :tau-source :selection-gain-only -- at 22 of 22 transitions (mean L_mix 19.185921 to 19.188693 against 19.179171 on S2). But a UNIFORM posterior scores 19.188231, beating two of the three arms and the default law both; and on S4 uniform beats every arm including the best. A law that loses to uniform is not shown better by that comparison, and a ranking that flips between the two fields of the same machine is not a ranking. What does survive as a fact about the machine: the default law's top candidate has a worse-than-field-average F_pi at 22 of 22 transitions (F@top -19.150441 against a field mean -19.1832), and under the decomposition below that is predominantly a statement about that candidate's declared variances."
                        :result-arms "The three arms are not three. :pi-only and :both put ln E in pi identically and differ only through gamma, so they share an argmax on 19 of 19 and 3 of 3 transitions and their L_mix differs by at most 2.083e-04 (S2) and 3.932e-05 (S4) -- 0.03 percent and 0.005 percent of the range. The separation that exists is :none against the other two (max |dL_mix| 2.785e-03, a different argmax on 22 of 22), which is the question of whether ln E enters pi AT ALL -- U3's question, which both sources answer yes -- and not the pi_0 placement question."
                        :why-the-vehicle-fails "THE COUNTERFACTUAL CONTROL. Re-scoring every arm against the observation the machine had ALREADY SEEN at tick t moves every arm's mean score by 1.701e-04 on S2 -- and the SPREAD of that movement across arms is 1.066e-14, so it changes no arm-against-arm comparison at all. On S4 the movement spread is 3.874e-04, still an order of magnitude larger than the whole :pi-only vs :both separation. THE MECHANISM: F_pi = SUM_ch 1/2 ln(2 pi v_ch) + SUM_ch 1/2 (o_ch - m_ch)^2 / v_ch. The first sum, which depends only on the candidate's declared variances, has a spread across candidates of exactly ln 2 = 0.693147 at every one of the 22 transitions -- 91.9 percent of F_pi's whole 0.754047 spread. The residual sum has spread 0.062500 and mean 0.0032 to 0.0043, and re-computing it against the previous observation moves it by at most 1.107e-03, nearly identically for every candidate. THE REASON: the three channels any candidate's action model predicts (:mission-health, :sorry-count-norm, :ticks-firing-ratio) are constant to 0.000000 across all 20 S2 ticks and all 4 S4 ticks, while the four that move (:loop-health 14 distinct, range 0.0234; :mathematics-pct, :portfolio-pct, :stack-pct 8 distinct each) are predicted by NO candidate and enter every candidate's F_pi at the same 0.01 variance floor. The observation genuinely varies -- 18 of 20 S2 observations are distinct, as C468 reported -- and varies only in coordinates orthogonal to every prediction on the field."
                        :typed-outcome :no-discrimination-score-is-outcome-independent
                        :not-claimed "No ruling. Nothing here says the variational law selects better or worse than the selection-gain fold; it says the vehicle SPEC U2 named cannot answer that on these fields. The recommendation this study carries is only the fallback SPEC U2 itself prescribed for a no-discrimination result: choose by source fidelity."
                        :what-would-answer-it "A field in which the channels the action model predicts actually move -- the same precondition as the selection-gain fold's :realized-outcome, which selection_gain.clj:185-193 records as ABSENT today and simulation-only, and the same obstruction RUN4 is blocked on. Length is NOT the missing thing: a 674-tick replay of this apparatus would carry the same 1e-14, and re-running this study longer is explicitly not recommended."}}
