  :pi-zero-form
  {:status :open-branches
   :statement "eq. 2.7's beta update is driven by (pi - pi_0) . G, so what pi_0 contains decides what the update measures. The sources disagree with themselves: friston2017.txt:684 gives pi_0 = sigma(-gamma . G) with no habit prior, while the authors' own implementation computes pu = spm_softmax(qE + w*Q) -- the habit prior IN pi_0 as well as in pi (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:964, verified in clone 530ec52). Our futon2.aif.policy-precision puts ln E in neither today."
   :arms {:habit-prior-in-both "SPM's form: ln E enters pi and pi_0 alike (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:963-964). (pi - pi_0) then isolates what F_pi alone does to the posterior, which is what the beta update is meant to measure."
          :habit-prior-in-pi-only "friston2017.txt:684 as printed: pi_0 = sigma(-gamma . G), no E. The beta update is then driven by the habit prior as well as by F_pi."}
   :measurement {:parameter "whether ln E, per candidate, is NON-UNIFORM over the aligned field the beta solve reads -- not whether selection applies it"
                 :withdrawn-parameter "whether ln E is applied to selection at all"
                 :withdrawal "That parameter was the wrong one, and the claim recorded under it -- the two arms COINCIDE on the live path and no recorded field can separate them -- is FALSE. It is withdrawn here rather than edited away. eq. 2.7's beta update does not consume the selection posterior: it builds its own pi and pi_0 out of G, F_pi and ln E (run7_beta_arms.clj:42-53), taking ln E from each candidate's :habit-prior-bias (run7_beta_arms.clj:95). The arms therefore separate whenever ln E is non-uniform over that field, whether or not selection ever reads it. Both things hold at once on our own S2 records: :habit-prior-applied? false on 20/20 decisions -- the strategic-recommendation branch war_machine.clj:4829-4837 asks for sets it so at policy.clj:306-307, and its chosen entry is the first non-no-op of the G-ordered list at policy.clj:283-285 -- AND ln E present on every aligned candidate, 3 distinct values, spread 3.0445 nats, no zeros, :habit-prior-source :learned-frequency on 143-145 of 145 candidates on every one of the 20 ticks. C3 stands; the inference drawn from C3 did not."
                 :values "SEPARATED on runs/2026-09-01-s2 -- see :run-result. Separated is not adjudicated: the three arms give three different gammas and all three converge and bracket on 20/20 ticks, and nothing measured here says which is better."
                 :control "the :none arm -- what converge-beta computes by default (:log-prior-placement :none, src/futon2/aif/policy_precision.clj) and what the S2 run itself recorded"
                 :what-would-adjudicate "a difference in what the machine SELECTS under each arm. That is an S3-stage measurement and not an S2 one, because gamma reaches selection only once FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE :variational-beta-gamma is wired (RUN8). Note before it is run: at today's selection boundary tau does not reach the selected action at all -- worklist I1 :slice-b2b gives the two code sites -- so the adjudicating measurement may have to change the boundary, or be a measurement of something other than the argmax."
                 :ships-behind-flag :habit-prior-in-both
                 :why "so that the arm shipped is stated, and is the one with the better rationale, while the entry stays open until an ADJUDICATING number exists. Recording a default is not deciding the choice."}
