   :u3-placement-comparison
   {:by "claude-cli" :at "2026-09-02" :row :U3 :report "C488-u3-pi-zero-placement.md"
    :script "u3_pi_zero_placement.clj:1-488" :artifact "U3-PI-ZERO-PLACEMENT.txt"
    :question-reached "THE MEASUREMENT :what-would-adjudicate NAMES -- a difference in what the machine SELECTS under each arm -- run at the one seam where the arms could reach a decision. The arms differ only in the eq. 2.7 beta they solve, and beta reaches selection by exactly one route: tau_eff = beta under :tau-mode :variational-beta-gamma (policy.clj:135-137). So the chain is arm -> beta_a(t) carried -> tau_a(t) -> softmax(ln E - G/tau - F_pi) (policy.clj:148) -> argmax, and every step below the solve uses the shipped function. NO DISCRIMINATION, TYPED BY MARGIN: 0 argmax differences out of 288 arm-tick comparisons (3 reachable score expressions x 4 beta_0 in {0.5,1,2,5} x 24 ticks: S2 20, S4 4). At the ONE site in the code where tau decides -- policy.clj:693-696, chosen-idx = argmax(ln E - G/tau) -- the choice survives a 13.599688-fold change in tau (lambda_break, computed in closed form: the score is linear in u = 1/tau, so the argmax is the upper envelope of lines and the window edge is the nearest crossing) while the three arms move tau by a factor of 1.074306 (rho, max over ticks at beta_0 = 1.0). Headroom 169.6x on S2 and 798.1x on S4, and monotone in beta_0: 34.9x at 0.5, 169.6x at 1.0, 901.9x at 2.0, 8343.3x at 5.0. At beta_0 = 1.0 not one candidate of 145 changes rank either, on :G or on ln E - G/tau."
    :arithmetic-floor "Under the ln-E-free, F_pi-free score the expression is -G/tau and argmax(-G/tau) = argmin G for EVERY tau > 0, so no beta whatever can move that law's choice. A fact about the expression, not about our field; CONTROL 4 checks it at nine tau from 1e-3 to 1e3 on 24 of 24 ticks rather than asserting it."
    :detector-has-teeth "The zeros are not a dead detector. Drop ln E from the SELECTION score while leaving F_pi in -- score -G/tau - F_pi -- and the placement starts deciding: 11 of 20 S2 ticks change argmax at beta_0 = 0.5, with lambda_break 1.043728 BELOW rho 1.166361, i.e. the arms move tau further than the choice survives. That expression is NOT REACHABLE: F_pi enters the posterior at the strategic boundary and nowhere else (policy.clj:634-638 throws otherwise) and that site always passes the full log-priors vector (policy.clj:553-556), built as zeros rather than nil (policy.clj:656-657) -- so F_pi without ln E requires an ln E identically zero, and ln E is non-zero on every aligned candidate here (3 distinct values, spread 3.0445224377 nats, 0 zeros, 24/24 ticks). It is reported as the shape of the null from the other side."
    :question-not-reached "THE DISCRIMINATOR SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U3 NAMED -- whether the in-pi-only arm brackets the H1b bound better -- does not exist on any committed field. Of the 24 records, 0 carry :act-gate-verdicts and 0 carry :realized-outcome; and H1b's restated bound has an antecedent occurring in 0 of the 50 records that DO carry gates (worklist :H1b :owner-did). No arm can be scored against it at any beta."
    :why-the-headroom-is-not-luck "ln E's 3.0445224377-nat spread over 3 groups is what holds the argmax down: within one ln E group the ordering is tau-invariant (the shift is monotone in G), so only cross-group pairs can flip and the nearest cross-group crossing sits 13.6x away. RUN8 found the same structure from the other direction -- runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt reports a smallest cross-group adjacent margin of 0.7355590795 with 0 argmax moves."
    :sharper-than-the-headroom "ON THE PATH THE RUNS ACTUALLY TOOK, beta reaches nothing that selects at all. All 24 records carry :selection-boundary :reason-bearing-strategic-policy, which is not one of select-action's boundaries: the controller decision's :action is REPLACED at war_machine.clj:5241-5244 by the mission the R14 strategic selector returned, and that selector is called (war_machine.clj:5211-5214) with a vector of three mission-id strings and a trace-id -- the strategic candidates in wm-admissible order (war_machine.clj:5203-5209), wm-admissible being the G-ordered ranked list filtered by executability (war_machine.clj:5169). No tau, no posterior, no score crosses that call. Measured from the records to match: the :decision :action equals the argmax of ln E - G/tau on 0 of 24 ticks. This is U1 readiness point 4 carried one call further, to the site that overwrites the action."
    :controls "1 SOLVER: the local generalised solver's :none arm against src converge-beta, max |delta| 0.000e+00 on 20 (S2) and 4 (S4) ticks, run before any arm is read. 2 RECORDED BETA: S2's own :beta-posterior reproduced from its own :beta-prior, max |delta| 0.000e+00 on 20 ticks; S4 recorded no :policy-precision-state and is reported NOT APPLICABLE rather than passed. 3 ENACTMENT: 0 of 24 gated, 0 of 24 realized. 4 TAU-INVARIANCE of the :G law, 24 of 24. 5 DETECTOR TEETH, above. The three arms also reproduce RUN7's gamma at S2 tick 20 independently (:none 0.9667979198, :pi-only 0.9040600731, :both 0.9712374387), so :run-result is now derived by two scripts from the same records."
    :bearing-on-the-ruling "RECOMMEND :habit-prior-in-both, and the entry STAYS :open-branches -- the ruling is Joe's. Three grounds in decreasing order of what the numbers carry. (1) The adjudicating measurement this entry specified has now been run at the seam this entry named and returns a typed no-discrimination result, 0 of 288 with 35x-8400x headroom and a detector shown able to fire. It does NOT say :both selects better; it says nothing the machine does distinguishes the arms, by a stated margin. (2) Under SPEC U2's fallback rule -- if the arms do not discriminate, choose by source fidelity -- the source is the authors' own implementation, which puts ln E in both (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:963-964, verified in clone by C463). That is already the :interim, so this changes nothing; it removes the reason the entry was open. (3) One ground that is measured and is about the arms rather than the field: :both leaves gamma 14 times closer to the ln-E-free arm than :pi-only does (|d gamma| at S2 tick 20 0.004440 against 0.062738), which is the near-cancellation the SPM rationale predicts and the reason (pi - pi_0) isolates F_pi. WHAT WOULD MAKE THE PLACEMENT DECIDABLE BY MEASUREMENT is not a longer replay: a selector that reads the posterior, and a field whose leaders sit within one ln E group of each other."
    :bounds "24 ticks, one route, one apparatus -- C486 section 7's bound. The lambda_break window is exact for the ARGMAX and says nothing about the rest of the ordering, which does move: 36-45 candidates change rank at beta_0 = 1.0 on the F_pi-bearing expressions. :G+F's unreachability is a reading of the call sites; a caller that passes a zero ln E vector alongside live F_pi would turn that control into a live case. The R14 selector was not chased into its own repo -- what is established is the SHAPE of its input at the futon2 call site and that the decision's action is replaced with its answer. And tau = beta is the only route from the arms to selection, so the whole comparison is conditional on the variational mode being the one that runs; S4 solved no beta of its own (:tau-source :selection-gain-only, tau = 1.0 on all 24 recorded ticks), so its arms use beta series this study solves."}
