  :selection-rule {:observed :argmax :status :resolved-by-source
                   :evidence "DETERMINISTIC, AND THE SOFTMAX WEIGHTS ARE NEVER SAMPLED, at every one of the four selection sites: policy.clj:809-812 (:actuation, no habit prior -- the head of the G-ordered list), policy.clj:838 (:actuation with a habit prior -- argmax of ln E - G/tau), policy.clj:593 (:strategic-recommendation -- head under :controller-head, argmax of ln E - G/tau_eff - F_pi under :full-score-posterior) and policy.clj:399-410 (default-mode-select, the try/catch fallback). C5's pointers (policy.clj:247-250, 387-410, 411-438) were re-anchored by U10 on 2026-09-02: 247-250 had drifted onto sorry-pressure-record and 411-438 onto decision-explanation, both of which kept resolving because pointer_check verifies line ranges and not content. No claim of C5's changed; the lines under it did."
                   :boundaries "WHICH BOUNDARY CONSULTS WHAT (U10, 2026-09-02). Recorded because 'the rule is argmax' was true of the posterior and false of the choice, and the entry did not say which. THREE SITES, and until U10 the score and the choice were the same expression at none of them. (i) :actuation without a habit prior (policy.clj:809-812): chooses the head of the G-ordered list; the recorded posterior is sigma(-G/tau), consulted by nothing. (ii) :actuation with a habit prior (policy.clj:838): chooses argmax(ln E - G/tau) -- a real argmax of a real score, but F_pi cannot reach this boundary (policy.clj:759-764 throws), so the F_pi term is absent by construction. (iii) :strategic-recommendation, THE ONE THE LIVE PATH TAKES (war_machine.clj:5377-5378): the F_pi-bearing posterior is recorded at policy.clj:668-670 and, under the default law :controller-head, read by nothing -- the choice is the G-ordered head at policy.clj:569,593. U10 adds the second law: under :selection-law :full-score-posterior the chosen action IS the argmax of that same posterior, taken from the same policy/selection-scores vector the posterior normalises (policy.clj:157-213, 563-567, 593), so the score and the choice are one expression rather than two that happen to agree."
                   :realised {:at "2026-09-02" :by "U10 (worklist.edn), SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U10"
                              :what "policy/selection-laws (policy.clj:503-519) is a closed two-member set; :selection-law reaches select-action as a declared option (policy.clj:749,754) and its two refusals are closed (policy.clj:765-781) and the live path as FUTON_WM_SELECTION_LAW (war_machine.clj:165-196: selection-law-of 165-182, arena-selection-law 184-196). Ties break to the first maximum (policy.clj:525-536) so a tie cannot read as a law change. The decision carries :selection-law {:requested :applied :refusal :controller-head-rank :chosen-rank :moved-from-controller-head?} (policy.clj:625-637), persisted with the decision (trace.clj:167-177) at trace-schema-version 22."
                              :default-unchanged "OFF BY DEFAULT. default-selection-law is :controller-head (policy.clj:520-524) and selection-law-of returns it for an unset OR unrecognised FUTON_WM_SELECTION_LAW (war_machine.clj:165-182), which is the same handling tau-mode-of gives. Pinned by selection-score-readiness-test/full-score-law-is-off-by-default-test on a field where the two laws choose differently, so the default is structurally off and not numerically lucky."
                              :fail-closed "TWO DIFFERENT FAILURES, TWO DIFFERENT ANSWERS. A law asked for when the flag chain can never produce F_pi is a config error and throws at the top of the tick (war_machine/selection-law-preconditions!, war_machine.clj:198-228, called at war_machine.clj:5311-5312 OUTSIDE the default-mode-select try/catch), because every tick would otherwise record a law it never ran. A per-tick coverage decline is NOT that: coverage is complete-or-off by design and 1 of S4's 4 ticks declined, so the selector takes the head it would have taken and records :selection-law :refusal with the envelope's own reason (policy.clj:582-593, 625-637). Throwing there would kill the tick, and -- because select-action is wrapped in a fallback -- kill it silently."
                              :measured-effect "ON THE THREE COMMITTED TICKS WHERE THE LAW CAN RUN, IT MOVES THE CHOICE ON ALL THREE. Replaying every recorded tick's own components through select-action under both laws (selection-score-readiness-test/chosen-action-attribution-on-the-recorded-fields-test): S4 ticks 0, 2 and 3 choose the rank-130 candidate where :controller-head takes the rank-1 head, with minimal mover set {ln E, F_pi} TOGETHER on each -- the same set the recorded posterior's argmax change attributes to, so posterior and choice now agree about what moved. The other 21 ticks fall back, and the two reasons are kept apart: S2's 20 ticks carry no :f-pi-posterior envelope at all (RUN7 dark carry, :no-f-pi-opts) and S4's remaining tick declines on :incomplete-coverage, 1 uncovered candidate of 145."
                              :not-reached "THE MODE DOES NOT MAKE THE MACHINE ACT ON THE FULL SCORE, and that is measured, not hedged: on 24 of 24 recorded ticks the action the RECORD carries is not this selector's output at all. war_machine.clj:5438 replaces the controller decision's :action with the mission the R14 strategic selector returned, and that selector is handed three mission-id strings and a trace id (war_machine.clj:5406-5410, the invoke-strategic-selection call) -- no tau, no posterior, no score crosses the call. U3 found this (see :choices :temperature-update :sharper-than-the-headroom); U10 wires the R6 seam and leaves the overwrite untouched, which was outside its acceptance. Pinned by the same test."
                              :flip-is-j-gated "NO FLIP IS MADE HERE and no ruling is written. The prediction the flip is to be judged against is stated BEFORE it in SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U10, U1-falsifier style, and the numbers above are the test's own literals, so a field that moves a different rank or a different term fails the suite rather than being read off a run afterwards."}
