  :c-grain {:observed :c-int-live-c-mis-built-and-off-by-default :status :observed-not-decided
            :evidence "TWO C's, ONE PER LOOP -- both in the code, only one of them live. C_int (interoceptive; the R19 stack; UNCHANGED by this design): normalised per-channel preference densities from preferences.clj:193 c-distribution -- [lo hi] range specs with exponential tails, {:becomes b} / {:p1 p} Bernoulli targets with temperature -- with risk a proper KL against them at preferences.clj:277-303, over the machine's own proprioception channels. C_mis (mission-grain), BUILT by U11 (futon2 3b8060a) and OFF BY DEFAULT: read-criteria (mission_c.clj:246-268) takes a mission's IDENTIFY completion criteria to {:criterion :observable :spec} rows, c-mis (mission_c.clj:270-315) builds {observable -> (pref/c-distribution spec)} with C_int's OWN constructor, log-c-mis (mission_c.clj:317-336) is the weighted log-sum composition and risk-mis (mission_c.clj:338-376) is the v0 term; the live readback is war_machine.clj:1557-1613 behind FUTON_WM_MISSION_C, attached by carry-mission-c (war_machine.clj:1615-1621) after every ranking and selection binding is final (war_machine.clj:5788-5799), persisted present-only at trace.clj:604-610. Design document: holes/labs/wm-contract/DESIGN-c-vector.md (claude-1 with Joe, 2026-09-02 evening)."
            :statement "C is a family indexed by loop grain, not one function. What runs live is C_int alone: every C the machine consults on a default tick is a preference over its own health channels, and the mission-grain C exists in the code and is read by nothing unless FUTON_WM_MISSION_C is set. Recorded as observed; the two-C split is a proposal awaiting Joe."
            :answers "The recorded S1 refusal -- 'a C over channels offered as a C over outcomes' (P-validated-R5.md:58; restated in futon3 at LA1c-restatement.md:543) -- and P-validated-R5 Q3 'what is C?', answered there as 'Unspecified. Scalar payoffs are scores, not a normalised preference distribution' (P-validated-R5.md:308). Naming the grain is what keeps the answer from being the refusal: C_int stays a C over channels and says so, C_mis is the C over mission outcomes, and the two meet only where a tick scores mission actions."
            :v0-forward-model "STATED PLAINLY, AND IT IS A HOLE RATHER THAN A SIMPLIFICATION: Q(o_k|pi) at mission grain does not exist, so v0 scores the STATUS QUO for every candidate (mission_c.clj:338-376) -- the per-criterion term is the surprisal -ln C_k at the CURRENT measured value of each observable, hence identical for every policy. DESIGN-c-vector.md section 3 argued this would still give a compliance gradient (the clocked mission's unmet criteria pulling G toward actions that address them). U12 measured that it does not."
            :measured "U12 (futon2 6110d5f; replay only over the three 2026-09-02 tick records 0a18c4f7, 4abad68c, 801976e7; artifacts holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/). Design section 7's falsifier returns (a) PASS with a named qualification -- the readback reproduces exactly from the three record fields, but the criteria arrive from an unhashed path so 'from record fields alone' is not yet true of a replay; (b) FAIL; (c) FAIL. SO THE v0 BINDING IS MEASURED NON-DISCRIMINATING, not an untested limitation: on each clocked tick 133 mission actions carry ONE distinct risk_mis value, 4.539889921682063E-5, the 13 non-mission actions carry no risk_mis field at all, and the clocked mission's own action carries the same value as the other 132. It does not vary with the world either -- a single-criterion sweep over all 14 channels R2 observes returns 1 distinct value -- and the cause is a type comparison, not the forward model: log-preference's Bernoulli branch selects the non-target outcome with (= 0 x) at preferences.clj:242-244, which is false for the double 0.0 R2 actually emits. Clause (c) fails by more than the temperature floor: at the double 0.0 the UNSATISFIED field scores the same 4.539889921682063E-5 as the satisfied one, so the completion gate section 3 argues for is not measurable on the live path at all. Design section 7's revert condition is therefore MET; nothing is flipped on, so the revert is a no-op today."
            :scalar-bridge "DESIGN-c-vector.md:125-136, recorded here because the p4ng defect-tally row :c-cost-vs-distribution (class 7, 'Duplicate representation unreconciled') carried the evidence 'no bridge'. THE BRIDGE: a scalar payoff is an affine image of log-C at the outcome the action targets, so a bare scalar in the codebase is a DECLARED PRIOR standing in for a log-density evaluation whose C has not been declared -- legitimate, and typed :scalar-awaiting-density rather than passed off as C. INSTANTIATED ONCE, at mission grain: mission_c.clj:317-336 composes ln C and the scalar risk_mis at mission_c.clj:338-376 is derived from it. APPLIED NOWHERE ELSE, which is why U13 moved the tally row to :partial and not to :repaired: :scalar-awaiting-density occurs in no source file (grep over ~/code for *.clj *.edn *.md *.lean, 2026-09-02 -- DESIGN-c-vector.md:131 and worklist.edn:693 only), and the scalars section 6 names are still bare: futon3c zaif_controller.clj:11-20, the uncalibrated Z2 arm constants, with the ask payoff (scale x EIG - operator-attention-cost) at zaif_controller.clj:87-96; and :expected-roi-gbp, built at war_machine.clj:1184-1197 and summed into a sustainability payoff at wm_regulator_sweep.clj:93-96."
            :lean-note "Design section 4 door 7: the C_mis records U11 writes are the live preference-stack evidence preferenceStackLiveRecorded (Holes.lean:6574-6575) wants, so its close-by-record path is NOTED and not taken -- no committed trace record carries a :mission-c key (grep over futon2 data/wm-trace/*.edn, 2026-09-02: zero files), because U11 and U12 both replayed and the flag is off by default."
            :nonnegativity "U17 (2026-09-02). OBSERVED, NOT RULED: this records the form the code now computes and the reason it was picked, in the shape :measured and :realised are written in; :status stays :observed-not-decided and no :choices key is added. THE HAZARD: under the v0 point-mass forward model the per-criterion term was the SURPRISAL -ln C_k(o_k). For a :bernoulli C that is the KL exactly (KL(delta_b || C) = -ln C(b) >= 0 because C(b) <= 1, pinned against pref/kl by mission_c_test/surprisal-is-the-point-mass-kl). For a :range C it is NOT a KL: a point mass has no density on a continuous support, KL(delta_x || C) is +infinity at every x, and what the code carried is the CROSS-ENTROPY gap/T + ln Z, fixed only up to an additive constant. A band narrower than one unit has Z < 1 and ln Z < 0, so a criterion read INSIDE its own declared band scored NEGATIVE -- -0.5119492459595545 for [0.5 1.0] at T = 0.1 (preferences_cdist_test/the-unshifted-range-term-is-the-negative-U17-names) -- and summing risk_mis into one G beside C_int's KL >= 0 would have paid a satisfied criterion a bonus. THE FORM CHOSEN, of the two U17 named: the EXCESS, KL(delta_x || C) - inf_y KL(delta_y || C) = gap/T, where the divergent point-mass entropy cancels between the two terms and ln Z with it (preferences.clj:375-439, point-mass-divergence-shift :415 and point-mass-divergence :429). NOT the clamp (max 0.0 (+ (/ gap T) log-z)), which also clears zero but flattens the gradient for a further -T ln Z outside the band (0.0512 for [0.5 1.0] at T = 0.1), reading a value that misses the band by 0.05 as fully satisfied; the excess form scores it 0.5 (mission_c_test/a-satisfied-range-criterion-no-longer-scores-below-zero). Same repair class as kl-gaussian-range (preferences.clj:441), which exists because 'the untruncated form was a divergence score that could dip below 0'. THE BERNOULLI BRANCH IS NOT SHIFTED, and that is the second half of the choice: its shift is 0.0, so subtracting its own minimum -ln max(p1, 1-p1) -- the 4.539889921682063E-5 T=0.1 satisfied floor U12 and U16 measured -- was NOT done. That floor is a real property of a soft target, not the missing-constant artefact the range branch has, and removing it would move numbers two committed replay artifacts pin. U12 clause (c)'s 'satisfied => zero' therefore stays unreached for Bernoulli criteria, exactly as U16 recorded. NO COMMITTED NUMBER MOVES: default-spec is {:becomes 1} (mission_c.clj:67-74) and no criterion in the corpus declares a :spec (U16), so divergence-shift (mission_c.clj:419) is 0.0 over the whole U12/U16 corpus and the range branch is so far reached only from tests. THE PRE-U17 NUMBER IS KEPT, NOT OVERWRITTEN: risk-mis records :cross-entropy (the unshifted sum) and :divergence-shift beside :risk, and per criterion :surprisal beside :divergence, so a reader can recover either form (mission_c.clj:436-501). ORTHOGONAL TO J6: the shift is a function of the spec KIND alone and never of which outcome an arm reads, so it is identical under every U16 arm and under none (mission_c_test/the-shift-is-the-same-under-every-arm). Also guarded: declared :criterion-weights must be finite and non-negative (mission_c.clj:322-338), because risk_mis >= 0 is a weighted sum of nonnegative terms and a negative weight would break the claim without touching a spec shape."
            :outcome-semantics-ruled "RULED BY JOE, 2026-09-02 (J6; recorded by U18, futon2 5af75e6). WHAT WAS ASKED: what IS a Bernoulli outcome when the observable is a continuous [0,1] channel? U12 found the shipped branch selects the non-target pole with (= 0 x), false for the double 0.0 R2 emits, so the unsatisfied pole was unreachable and an unread nil scored as the target (preferences.clj:292; it was :242-244 when U12, U13 and :flip-is-j-gated below were written, and futon2 5af75e6 moved log-preference down the file -- those earlier pointers now resolve to different lines, and re-anchoring text a signature covers is not something this row does silently). U16 BUILT AND RAN the three candidate readings over the U12 corpus and the 14-channel sweep -- :numeric-equality 14/14 measured with 2 distinct risks, :declared-binarization 4/14, :typed-binary-only 0/14 (runs/U16-outcome-semantics/) -- and none was preferable on any number, because ranking them needs to know whether a criterion like U-rows green is a binary observable and no field records that. THE RULING: arm 2, :declared-binarization. A Bernoulli spec on a continuous observable must carry a threshold; an observable DECLARED binary needs none; anything else is REFUSED rather than scored. THE GROUNDS, AND THE CHANNEL EXACTLY AS IT HAPPENED, because the assent was to a linked framing and not to the arm's name: claude-1 presented the three arms with the recommendation 'arm 2, because the declaration work it demands is the same edit you already have pending', and Joe answered 'add the criteria to the doc'. The first execution of the ruling is that edit -- futon2 161ac09 ports the punch-in IDENTIFY criteria into holes/missions/M-zaif-harness-v1.md with each observable declared BINARY, U12's planted channel bindings explicitly excluded. J6 :ruling and :bar carry the full record. WHAT THE RULING COSTS, recorded beside it rather than left implicit: it buys a typed absence on nearly every tick until the mission documents are amended, where :numeric-equality would have bought a number on every tick at the price of reading 0.75 as a MET criterion. J6's 0.75-consequence note therefore does NOT apply -- arm 2 refuses an undeclared continuous observable rather than scoring it -- and the price is paid in documentation work on nine criteria across two missions. Measured, at the ruling: replaying the three 2026-09-02 records under the ruled default returns :absent :unread-outcome where the pre-ruling path returned 4.539889921682063E-5, because no criterion in that corpus declares a spec; the same replay repairs U12 clause (c), whose :unsatisfied-double-0.0 moves from 4.539889921682063E-5 to 10.000045398900184. IMPLEMENTED (U18): mission-c/default-outcome-semantics (mission_c.clj:86) is the arm and is what log-c-mis and risk-mis take when :outcome-semantics is omitted; an EXPLICIT nil still names the pre-ruling raw path, kept reachable only so U16's :v0-shipped comparison column reproduces what it measured. THE DECLARATION'S HOME MOVED, which is J6's acceptance and not a free choice: a criterion's own :spec carries :observable-kind and :threshold, pref/c-distribution carries them onto the built distribution present-only, and log-preference-under merges the SPEC's declaration OVER the caller's selector -- a per-call selector may fill a declaration the mission omits and may not overrule one it wrote down. GAUGES ARE DECLARED, NOT PLANTED: war-machine/mission-c-declared-gauges binds each of M-zaif-harness-v1's three criteria to the observable it is read from, every criterion row built from one carries :observable-source :declared-gauge and a pointer back to the declaration, and the readback records :declared-gauges and :outcome-semantics so a number says which bindings and which reading produced it. Read under those gauges the mission's three criteria are 3/3 :measurable and score for the first time. NOTHING NEW IS DECIDED HERE. This key records a ruling that was made, with its grounds and its price; the two-C split above is still :observed-not-decided, FUTON_WM_MISSION_C is still off, and the flip remains Joe's."
