  :focus-clock-reconciliation
  {:observed :recorded-divergence-flag-gated-default-off :status :observed-not-decided
   :question "WHICH mission's C parameterizes the tick's G when the machine's own selection and its witnessed clock edge name different missions -- and what the tick records when they do. G imports C (dacosta2020 eq. 44), and the formalism does not say which mission supplies it; that is the free hand. U11 wired C_mis to the CLOCKED mission, U21 wired it to the SELECTED one behind FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS, and neither says what happens when the two disagree -- which they do on 3 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 ticks."
   :statement "The seam: load-active-mission reads the durable clock at the TOP of the tick (war_machine.clj:1549) and record-selection-clock! writes the new edge AFTER the trace is persisted (war_machine.clj:1986), inside a `future` whose failure is printed to stderr and dropped. So the focus a tick reads is the PREVIOUS tick's selection, and -- this is the part U21 left open -- a durable edge that is one tick stale because the write LANDED and one that is stale because the write NEVER LANDED read identically from inside a tick. U21 recorded the relation as one boolean, :agrees-with-durable?, which returns false for at least four different states including one where the durable side was never read at all (FUTON_WM_CLOCK_FOCUS off makes active-mission nil, so the projection is compared against {})."
   :options {:same-tick-witnessed-edge
             "Write the clock edge synchronously before the trace, so the two sides agree by construction. REJECTED: it changes what a clock edge MEANS (a witness of a persisted decision becomes a witness of an intention), puts a substrate write on the tick's critical path ahead of the trace, and does not solve the case the row was minted for -- it moves the write's failure earlier, into the tick, rather than removing it. The row's own statement puts edge-minting out of scope: `a clock edge is witnessed evidence, and any minting this row proposes needs its witness rule named`."
             :typed-pending-state
             "Record :pending on every mission selection until the write is witnessed. REJECTED: the tick cannot observe its own future's completion, and nothing in the tick ever resolves the pending state, so every mission tick would carry a :pending that only a LATER tick could clear -- which is option three with an extra field. It relocates the silence rather than removing it."
             :recorded-divergence-cleared-by-a-later-tick
             "CHOSEN. The tick records a typed divergence and the next tick says whether the previous tick's write landed, read off a witness rather than assumed: the clock edge already carries witness.source, the identity of the trace record whose selection caused it (clock-source, war_machine.clj:1977), and the tick already holds the previous trace record. Comparing them answers `did the previous write land?` with evidence. It requires no new write, mints no edge, and makes the currently-dropped failure visible in the record."}
   :grounds "The two rejected options both write or promise a write; only the third turns a silent failure into a recorded one without changing what a clock edge means. The discriminator is not new evidence -- witness.source has been stamped on every edge since S4 and was simply dropped by the read (active-clock-edge->mission, war_machine.clj:1525-1548, now keeps it under this flag)."
   :evidence "IMPLEMENTED, DEFAULT OFF. Flag: war_machine.clj:125 *focus-reconcile?* / FUTON_WM_FOCUS_RECONCILE. Shared identity rule used by both sides of the seam, so writer and reader cannot drift: trace-record-identity war_machine.clj:1610-1618, delegated to by clock-source at war_machine.clj:1977-1984. Closed eight-case vocabulary: focus-reconciliation-cases war_machine.clj:1631-1667. Reconciler: focus-reconciliation war_machine.clj:1669-1738, attached by tick-mission-focus war_machine.clj:1740-1783 and called once at war_machine.clj:6195-6196 with the previous trace record. Render (half b): render-mission-focus-line war_machine.clj:4068-4109, appended at war_machine.clj:4126-4128 AFTER the untouched render-active-mission-line war_machine.clj:4058-4066, so the durable clock and the tick's focus are two lines and never one. Tests: war_machine_test.clj:2022-2247. Replay over the three 2026-09-02 records: holes/labs/wm-contract/u43_focus_reconcile.clj, artifacts under holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U43-focus-reconcile/."
   :measured "All eight cases produced what they declared (the script exits 1 if any does not). On the LIVE corpus no record reaches :lagged-write-landed or :lagged-write-missing, and that is the finding rather than a gap in the replay: the S4 read dropped witness.source until this row, so no persisted :active-mission carries the discriminating field and the honest reading of all three records is :lag-unattributable -- the divergence is real and its cause is not yet measurable. Record 0a18c4f7 reads :no-durable-edge; 4abad68c and 801976e7 read :lag-unattributable. U21's boolean returns false on all three AND on :clock-not-read, :durable-unreadable and :no-durable-edge, which is why the case vocabulary is added BESIDE it and does not replace it."
   :flip-is-j-gated "NO FLIP IS MADE AND NO RULING IS WRITTEN. FUTON_WM_FOCUS_RECONCILE defaults off (war_machine.clj:125); with it off, tick-mission-focus returns U21's map unchanged and the S4 clock read keeps its exact four-key shape (pinned by war_machine_test.clj:2022-2049). The reconciliation is computed from wm-decision and the previous trace record, both already final where they are bound, and attached after ranking and selection, so no rank, weight, temperature, admissibility verdict or selector can read it."
   :not-claimed "NOT ADJUDICATED, and one thing explicitly NOT repaired. :observed records that the divergence is now typed and the dropped write is now visible; no number here says the chosen option is better than the two rejected ones, and none of them has been run live. record-selection-clock! remains a fire-and-forget future whose failure is printed to stderr and dropped -- a tick that records :lagged-write-missing does not re-attempt the write. Repairing the write (a retry, or a same-tick witnessed edge) would change what a clock edge means and needs its own witness rule named; it is out of this row's scope and is not minted as a row here."
   :provenance "U43, minted by U21. Choice-set registration under TN-edge-review-aif-wiring section 1 point 3, NOT a ruling (Joe 2026-09-01 rule): it records what the War Machine is observed to do behind a default-off flag. Related: :c-grain, which registers WHICH C runs live; this entry registers which MISSION supplies it when the two candidate sources disagree."}

