  :selection-retrospective
  {:observed :rationale-recorded-never-scored :status :observed-not-decided
   :question "The machine records WHY it chose what it chose, and nothing ever asks whether that reason held up. Joe, 2026-09-03, dictated in session: when the machine refuses to work on a given piece of work, are we logging that rationale and learning whether the rationale holds up -- does it maybe regret that choice -- we need to really focus on that learning loop aspect. Joe states NO strong prior on the right form, so this entry registers a choice-set and rules on nothing. The free hands are three: what a selection-time rationale ASSERTS (so that it can be contradicted), what evidence SCORES it, and where a refuted one goes."
   :statement "Two refusal channels exist and only one of them says why. ADMISSION: policy-support-exclusions carries a typed reason per refused candidate -- 376 refusals over the 94 ranking-bearing records, 4 per tick, every one :mission-absent-from-capability-graph, never scored. SELECTION: everything below the chosen entry in the controller ranking -- 144 to 146 candidates per tick, so about 145 rejections per tick, with NO reason field, though the full per-candidate G decomposition (G-risk, G-ambiguity, G-goal-outcome, augmentation-terms, habit-prior-bias, and the mission factors on the action) is recorded beside it. A primitive regret signal exists: previous-selection-non-progress? war_machine.clj:2312-2326 and recent-non-progress-count war_machine.clj:2339-2356, decaying mission value by non-progress-decay-k war_machine.clj:2290."
   :measured "THE CARRIER DISJOINTNESS, which is what shapes the form. Over the whole trace corpus (56 files, 885 records): 94 records carry [:decision :controller-ranking], 88 carry [:realized-outcome], and ZERO carry both -- the ranking era is 2026-08-30 to 09-02 and the outcome era is 2026-07-02 to 07-06. No record in the corpus reaches any of the three places trace-outcome looks (war_machine.clj:2328-2332), so the non-progress signal can never read that progress happened on the tick path; the :grounded-change it tests for is written by a different producer. Further, all 88 :realized-outcome maps carry :expected-G/:realized-G, while fold-realized-outcome (selection_gain.clj:196-206) admits a sample only on numeric :expected-score AND :realized-score, so 0 of 88 are foldable and :samples is 0 on all 125 records carrying a gain state; the correctly shaped producer exists at fold_realized.clj:96-100 and is not what wrote them. THE PRIMITIVE SIGNAL'S REACH, measured: on 2026-09-01 the machine ran 79 ticks over exactly two missions in strict alternation; of 11455 candidate rows exactly 79 carry a decay -- one per tick, always the immediately previous selection -- the count reaches 2 on no row, and the chosen action's own :non-progress-count is 0 on all 79 ticks. The walk terminates at the first record naming a different target (the :else arm), so one intervening selection forgives the count: measured on 2026-09-02, M-wm-aif-policy-grain-compliance carries count 1 / decay 0.5 at 14:00 and is back to 0 / 1.0 at 14:03."
   :form-candidates
   {:a-rationale-as-claim "A typed record projected from fields already on the trace record -- chosen, top-k rejected, the per-term margin decomposition, the term carrying most of it, and the counter-channel that favoured a rejected candidate without being consulted (lnE enters the selected score only under :full-score-posterior, policy.clj:582 and :593, recorded as :habit-authority at policy.clj:619-621). NO NEW LOGGING: :claim/derived-from names seven recorded fields and nothing else. The claim also refuses to mint on a record whose own :selection-law contradicts its ranking, which is a measured case and not a hypothetical: run 0a18c4f7 says :chosen-rank 1 / :moved-from-controller-head? false with the chosen action at controller rank 124, the false stamp recorded at S4-identify-ingest.edn:40."
    :b-retrospective-evaluator "A verdict keyed to the claim id and a window, over four legs. Measured today: OVERTAKE only. Typed absent: C_mis movement (the U18/U42 readback is keyed to the tick's SELECTED mission, so two ticks selecting different missions have two subjects and no movement; :measured on 1 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 runs), and RECEIPTS attributable to the hold (:no-mission-to-receipt-carrier; U23 measured flight-discharge as :writer-exists-no-records and clocked-on as recording who clocked on, not what landed). Closed verdict vocabulary :rationale-upheld / :rationale-refuted / :rationale-untestable {:reason}; :rationale-upheld is unreachable on this corpus because it needs an outcome leg."
    :c-tension-mint "Only a REFUTED verdict mints, and it mints into U41's record and not a new one: DESIGN-tensions-as-patterns.md section 3 already owns the shape and already names :tension/born-of :refuted-rationale as one of its three sources. This entry adds only the mint edge -- poles derived from the claim's :lost-on term, statement carrying both run-ids, status :carried, resolution-path :none-named-at-mint. The library home is NAMED AND NOT WRITTEN TO: the WM's addressable pattern artifact is a .flexiarg under futon3/library (pattern_registry.clj:48-53, resolved by pattern_registry.clj:158-161), and the birth rule requires two typed receipts and a person."}
   :verdict-rule-options
   {:overtake-dominant "Any overtake refutes. REJECTED HERE ON A MEASUREMENT, not on taste: on the recorded 2026-09-02 pair it refutes every claim after one tick, because the chosen mission's mission-value-factor halves by construction (0.59 to 0.295, non-progress-decay 1.0 to 0.5) while every rival's factor is byte-identical. Such a test measures the decay, not the rationale."
    :weighted-legs "Combine the four legs with declared weights. REJECTED HERE: three of the four legs are typed absences on this corpus, so the weights would be unmeasurable and would be fiat standing in for measurement."
    :declared-attributed-overtake "CHOSEN AS THE FORM TO PUT FORWARD, and declared rather than ruled. REFUTED iff some candidate the claim rejected later out-ranked the chosen one AND its own recorded movement alone would have closed the asserted margin; an overtake that happens only because the chosen candidate was decayed is UNTESTABLE. Two booleans read off the records, NO tunable scalar. It discriminates on the recorded corpus: of the four top rejected candidates that out-ranked M-zaif-harness-v1 one tick later, exactly one (M-expressions-of-interest, own G-core fall 0.005237161 against the 0.004028678 it was rejected by) survives the attribution; the other three read :chosen-decayed."}
   :learning-feed "VERDICTS ACCUMULATE AS EVIDENCE; NO LIVE WEIGHT MOVES WITHOUT A J-GATE. Four parts: (1) a verdict is appended to a ledger under runs/ and written into no trace record, no registry entry and no store; (2) nothing in the tick may read the ledger -- ranking, temperature, admissibility verdicts and selector must be byte-identical whether it exists or not, the containment mission_gauges.clj already states for its own observables; (3) the three consumers are all offline -- the Z3-style pre-registered A/B, arm C :cascade-catalog-playout of :task-belief-actand-source, and Joe's review; (4) any change that lets a verdict influence a live number (a weight, non-progress-decay-k, a tau feed, an admissibility rule) is a worklist :J row and Joe's call. This row does not mint that J row; it names the boundary the row would have to cross."
