   :evidence "DESIGN PASS ONLY -- nothing implemented on the live path, no file under src/ or scripts/futon2/ changed. Producer (read-only; no tick, no run lock, no substrate call, no network, nothing written under data/): holes/labs/wm-contract/u39_selection_retrospective.bb, run from the futon2 root with bb. Design doc and both artifacts under holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U39-selection-retrospective/ (README.md, u39-measurements.edn, U39-SELECTION-RETROSPECTIVE.txt), byte-identical on two consecutive runs. Four controls, all pass: a fabricated mission id appears in no record and in no claim; every claim margin reproduces the recorded controller-score difference at max absolute deviation 0.0; the overtake detector does not fire on a record scored against itself; it does fire on the recorded 2026-09-02 pair."
   :not-claimed "NO RULING, and four things explicitly not done. The verdict rule is :declared-not-ruled with its alternatives named. No retrospective is run over history beyond the one worked pair -- that is worklist :U40, which is :blocked and builds on this shape. The tension record is not implemented -- that is :U41. Nothing is written to the pattern library. Also NOT repaired here, and recorded so it is not mistaken for a finding of this row: the :expected-G / :expected-score key mismatch is an era artifact of a superseded writer, not a defect in the shipped fold, and the non-progress walk's alternation behaviour is described rather than changed."
   :provenance "U39, minted from Joe's 2026-09-03 dictation. Choice-set registration under TN-edge-review-aif-wiring section 1 point 3, NOT a ruling: it records what the War Machine is observed to do and names the form candidates. claude-2 review invited on the arm-C consumer side, per the row's acceptance. Related entries: :focus-clock-reconciliation, whose one-tick clock lag is why :tension/carried-by reads the previous tick's mission in the worked example; :c-grain, which registers which C runs live and so bounds the C_mis leg; :task-belief-actand-source, whose arm C is the offline consumer named in :learning-feed."}
